Embodied Cosmogenesis

Pantheon handles: Umwelt Theology, The Sensorium Makes the Sacred, Gods of the Interface
Status: Provisional canonical module
Epistemic status: Comparative thought experiment grounded in animal sensory ecology; not a claim that nonhuman animals possess religion in the human sense.

1. Core claim

An embodied intelligence does not begin with reality in full. It begins with the reality its body can detect, remember, act upon, and survive within. Recurrent forces inside that accessible world become salient; salient forces become compressed into symbols, practices, prohibitions, and sacred order.

> A mind builds metaphysics from the invariants its body can detect.

Canonical pipeline:

```text
body and habitat
→ available senses and actions
→ experienced world (Umwelt)
→ recurrent powers, absences, and uncertainties
→ sacred distinctions
→ ritualized responses
→ cosmology
```

Reverse inference:

```text
cosmology or ritual
→ sacred distinction
→ recurrent uncertainty
→ perceptual/action interface
→ probable body, habitat, and social structure
```

Religion is therefore treated here as an interface report: a compressed account of what a kind of mind repeatedly encounters, cannot fully control, and cannot afford to ignore.

