13. Reverse Umwelt Inference

Pantheon handles: Reverse Zookeeper, Known Asymmetry Laboratory, Echoes Above the Waterline
Status: Provisional operator extension
Purpose: Use known interactions between humans and other organisms to derive testable signatures of forces that may exceed human senses, causal reach, spatial scale, temporal scale, or conceptual ontology.

13.1 Core distinction

The analogy licenses possibility generation, not ontological promotion.

```text
Known higher-layer interaction
→ remove privileged knowledge of the higher layer
→ retain only lower-layer observations
→ extract the observable signature
→ transpose the signature to human-scale anomalies
→ generate competing explanations
→ derive discriminating predictions
→ test
→ update
```

Constitutional statement:

> Similarity tells us what might be possible. Prediction and differential evidence tell us what is actually there.

13.2 The known-side inversion

For a human affecting an animal:

```text
human objective H
→ action/intervention A
→ environmental transformation E
→ animal-accessible trace O
→ animal response B
```

The animal generally lacks direct access to H and may have only partial access to A. It encounters E and O and must infer whatever it can through survival, learning, or inherited adaptation.

Now place humanity in the lower-layer position:

```text
unknown source X
→ unknown mechanism M
→ human-accessible trace O_h
→ hypothesis set {natural, emergent, distributed, agentic}
→ intervention/probe P
→ return O_h'
→ delta
```

The same observable trace may be generated by multiple hidden causes. Therefore:

```text
trace similarity ≠ source identity
```

