```

13.12 Failure modes

1. Agency inflation: every unexplained regularity becomes an intentional actor.
2. Natural-law anthropomorphism: constraints are interpreted as rules imposed for our benefit or punishment.
3. Narrative overfit: a story explains existing observations but risks no future prediction.
4. Single-analogy capture: one human–animal relationship dominates the candidate ontology.
5. Selection blindness: striking anomalies are remembered while silent non-events disappear.
6. Scale collapse: distributed, emergent, and centralized agency are treated as equivalent.
7. Instrument naïveté: measurement artifacts are attributed to the observed world.
8. Reciprocity assumption: an impactful force is assumed capable of receiving or understanding our response.
9. Identity leap: evidence for an unknown mechanism is presented as evidence for a named source.
10. Hostile/benevolent projection: local harm or benefit is treated as evidence of global intention.
11. Unbounded recursion: every failed prediction creates another invisible layer rather than lowering confidence.
12. Anthropic privilege: human salience is mistaken for the objective center of the process.

Hard gates:

```text
RUI-G1: anomaly is not mechanism
RUI-G2: mechanism is not agency
RUI-G3: agency is not consciousness
RUI-G4: consciousness is not identity
RUI-G5: local consequence is not global objective
RUI-G6: a failed risky prediction must reduce confidence
RUI-G7: every promoted claim retains provenance and viable alternatives
RUI-G8: unknown does not mean unknowable, supernatural, or agentic
```

13.13 Reality-rent requirement

Reverse Umwelt Inference becomes useful only when it pays at least one form of reality rent:

• reveals a previously unmeasured variable,
• predicts a future observation,
• improves instrument placement,
• separates competing causal models,
• discovers a scale mismatch,
• exposes an interface artifact,
• changes a safe decision,
• or establishes a justified stopping rule.

Under the RFHL rule:

```text
value = Novel Delta × Reusability × Reach × Reality
```

If Reality = 0, the result remains imaginative material rather than validated edge.

